0..76 Comment "// The pure λ-calculus as data and its single substitution, the base of the"
77..144 Comment "// λ-calculus syntax model. `theory LC` is the single-substitution"
145..222 Comment "// calculus of Kaposi and Xie (_Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories_,"
223..292 Comment "// FSCD 2024, doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10, §7): the presentation"
293..367 Comment "// `first_order` mints from `theory Lambda`, its names written without the"
368..440 Comment "// generated `$` and its context arguments implicit, as a `theory` block"
441..508 Comment "// writes them. The syntax model\'s carriers are de Bruijn terms and"
509..584 Comment "// two substitution data: a substitution shifts, conses a term onto another"
585..661 Comment "// or lifts one under a binder, and a renaming shifts or lifts. Lifting is a"
662..733 Comment "// constructor, so the substitution laws reach their inductive steps by"
734..798 Comment "// conversion; lifting written as a definition reaches them too."
799..801 Comment "//"
802..877 Comment "// The argument, file by file: this base; the laws that hold by computation"
878..954 Comment "// (`sub-q-single`, `sub-q-lift`, `sub-lam`, `sub-app`); the congruences and"
955..1028 Comment "// the lemmas laws 3 and 4 are proved from (`congruence`, `shift-lookup`,"
1029..1096 Comment "// `rename-rename`, `lookup-weaken`, `subst-rename`, `subst-subst`,"
1097..1166 Comment "// `lift-as-definition`, `subst-id`, `subst-as-rename`); laws 3 and 4"
1167..1228 Comment "// (`sub-weaken-lift`, `sub-weaken-single`); the syntax model"
1229..1294 Comment "// (`syntax-model`) and the record of `LC`\'s models it packs into"
1295..1315 Comment "// (`model-record`)."
1316..1318 Comment "//"
1319..1333 Comment "// - see: #640"
1334..1349 Comment "// - see: #2422"
1351..1390 Comment "// The naturals, the de Bruijn indices."
1391..1397 Keyword "import"
1398..1399 StringLit "\""
1399..1423 StringLit "../model-in-source.gandr"
1423..1424 StringLit "\""
1424..1425 Other ";"
1427..1498 Comment "/// The single-substitution calculus of the pure λ-calculus: contexts,"
1499..1572 Comment "/// substitutions between them and terms in a context; the empty context,"
1573..1648 Comment "/// substitution, context extension, weakening, the newest variable, single"
1649..1715 Comment "/// substitution and lifting; abstraction and application; the six"
1716..1790 Comment "/// substitution laws. Law 3 moves a weakening past a lift and back, so no"
1791..1868 Comment "/// path order orients it and the rules are refused; `Model(LC)` derives from"
1869..1896 Comment "/// the block all the same."
1897..1899 Other "@["
1900..1907 Other "refuses"
